# ==============================================================================
# DevSecOps .dockerignore
# Purpose: Prevent sensitive credentials from leaking into Docker images,
# reduce Docker build context transfer time, and eliminate non-production artifacts.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Dependency & Debug Artifacts (Build Optimization & Integrity)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prevents transferring host-installed node_modules with potentially incompatible
# host architectures or infected modules; dependencies are built freshly in Stage 1.
node_modules
# Excludes local npm error and debug logs containing host system paths and details.
npm-debug.log*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Version Control & Repository Metadata (Security & Context Optimization)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prevents leaking git commit history, contributor emails, commit hashes, or secrets
# committed in past revisions; significantly decreases Docker build context size.
.git
.gitignore

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Environment Variables & Secret Manifests (Critical Security Control)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Strictly blocks all local environment configurations containing database credentials,
# secret keys, tokens, and passwords from becoming baked into immutable image layers.
.env
.env.*
# Whitelist only the non-sensitive configuration template for reference.
!.env.example

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Container Build & Orchestration Definitions (Context Optimization)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Avoids unnecessary circular references and recursive container configuration files.
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yaml

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Documentation & Markdown Files (Context Optimization & Attack Surface Reduction)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excludes documentation files which are not required for production container runtime.
README.md
*.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Test Suites, Coverage & Internal Automation (Security & Image Footprint)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prevents test fixtures, mocks, vulnerability scripts, and test data from runtime access.
tests/
# Excludes internal operational/deployment shell scripts from container image layers.
scripts/
# Excludes local demonstration material.
demo/
# Excludes architectural and API documentation assets.
docs/
# Excludes generated build and analysis artifacts.
artifacts/
# Excludes code coverage reports and test metrics.
coverage/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. CI/CD Workflows, Kubernetes Manifests & Developer Tooling
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excludes GitHub Actions workflows and automation runners.
.github/
# Infrastructure-as-Code manifests belong in orchestrators, not inside the API image.
k8s/
# Excludes local IDE metadata, editor settings, and workspace preferences.
.vscode/
.idea/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Local Binaries & Host Executables (Security & Integrity)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excludes host-specific management utilities and Windows/Linux executables.
kubectl.exe
